From: JustinPringle <justin.j.pringle@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:27:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Explorer: timetable clash rule (TTC-v1), synced from
 reg_advisor

Vendor reg_advisor's timetable clash rule and mirror it on the page. Two
modules that share a lecture period cannot both be registered; the student
takes the lower-level one first.

- vendor_sync.py carries catalogue/timetable.yaml; re-synced engine,
  loader and programme YAMLs from reg_advisor (TTC-v1).
- build_explorer.py passes the timetable explicitly and refuses to build
  without it; ships the timetable and rules.timetable in the payload; module
  levels now come from the engine (ENPD7PP and ENPD7CL read L4, per ITS).
- ra_engine.js mirrors find_clashes and apply_timetable; adviseAll gives
  the page eval_advice's whole-set verdicts. A new parity profile exercises
  a clash; parity 595/595.
- The page shows a CLASH verdict, explains it in the inspector, draws a
  leader to the lower-level module, and lists it on the advisory record.

